From 631d10b921c4ff93407c1dfcca9c2919b47b267d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:48:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: IMSI paging detector (T-OR-056)

ImsiPagingAnalyzer (default off) flags a PCCH paging record that addresses
a UE by its permanent IMSI rather than a temporary S-TMSI. A false base
station pages a known IMSI to confirm a target's presence without an attach.

Reported Medium, not High: normal paging uses the S-TMSI, but MME
failure/restoration can legitimately fall back to paging by IMSI (TS 23.401
5.3.4.3, TS 23.007 20), and this analyzer cannot yet tell whether the paged
IMSI is this device's -- that salted-hash compare (needing the device IMSI
over AT) is follow-up T-OR-116 and would raise a confirmed self-page.

Reads only the identity type, never the paged digits (the in-memory
identity contract in docs/ANALYZERS.md). Stateless; off by default pending
per-network calibration. Test vectors are PCCH Paging PDUs encoded with the
reference Python pycrate and decoded through telcom_parser: paging by IMSI
(fires Medium, digits never in the event), an IMSI record after an S-TMSI
record (exercises the multi-record path), paging by S-TMSI (ignored), a
Paging with no records (ignored), and a non-PCCH LTE message (ignored).

